      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Suppose we want to measure the volume of a chocolate box. What units could we use?",
      "worked_solution": "We can measure length in centimeters $(\\text{cm}).$ When measuring lengths in centimeters, volumes are measured in $\\text{cm}\\times \\text{cm}\\times \\text{cm},$ which is usually written as ${\\text{cm}}^{3}.$",
