      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Suppose we want to determine the area of the largest airport in the world. What units could we use?",
      "worked_solution": "We can measure length in miles $(\\text{mi}).$ When measuring lengths in miles, areas are measured in $\\text{mi}\\times \\text{mi},$ which is usually written as ${\\text{mi}}^{2}.$",
