    "q-144174": {
      "dom_id": "step-q144174",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14144298/assets/0c9e721ad5458931b15f8f255f17b9ce02b7973f25e791278da18f4f8997ac68.png)\n\nWhat is the area of the square above?",
      "worked_solution": "To calculate the area $A$ of a square, we square its side length. Therefore, the area of the square is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =(7\\,\\text{cm})^{2} \\\\  & =7\\,\\text{cm}\\times 7\\,\\text{cm} \\\\  & =(7\\times 7)\\times (\\text{cm}\\times \\text{cm}) \\\\  & =49\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
