    "q-171696": {
      "dom_id": "step-q171696",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "The area of a square with a side length of $9\\,\\text{cm}$ is{{field-1}}\n${\\text{cm}}^{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To calculate the area $A$ of a square, we square its side length. Therefore, the area of the square is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =(9\\,\\text{cm})^{2} \\\\  & =9\\,\\text{cm}\\times 9\\,\\text{cm} \\\\  & =(9\\times 9)\\times (\\text{cm}\\times \\text{cm}) \\\\  & =81\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
